WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.375
Every channel in America is marked on one idea, and it fits in three words.

2
00:00:05.625 --> 00:00:07.725
Red, right, returning.

3
00:00:07.975 --> 00:00:11.600
Keep the red marks on your right side when you’re returning.

4
00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:13.850
But returning from where?

5
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.200
From seaward, heading in.

6
00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:18.400
Or heading upstream.

7
00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:30.600
And along the coast, where there’s no in or out, it means traveling clockwise around the country: south down the Atlantic coast, north up Florida’s Gulf coast, then west along the Gulf.

8
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:32.675
Look at the diagram.

9
00:00:32.925 --> 00:00:37.725
The red buoys are nuns, with pointed tops, and they carry even numbers.

10
00:00:37.975 --> 00:00:42.025
The green buoys are cans, flat on top, with odd numbers.

11
00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:45.050
And the numbers get bigger as you head in.

12
00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:50.500
So you’re running out of the channel toward the Gulf, and there’s a red nun ahead.

13
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.850
Which side do you leave it on?

14
00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.525
Your left.

15
00:00:54.775 --> 00:00:57.400
Going out, everything reverses.

16
00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:00.800
Red, right, returning, and only returning.
